            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The pads fall into three clear groups. Consumer pads from $133 to about $365 are what most home workers
            buy, and they are fine for an hour or two a day at a slow walk. Office-grade bases from LifeSpan, at $1,199
            to $1,699, are built and rated for long daily use with wide 20-inch belts. The Unsit, at $2,345 to $2,595,
            is a specialist: very wide, very slow and capped at 2 mph by design. Unbranded pads also sat at $85 to $100
            on Amazon the same day; their listings rarely state a duty rating or warranty, which is what you are buying
            when a pad will run for hours. Our <a href="/under-desk-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">under desk treadmills</a> guide compares the office-grade models in more detail.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="standing-desks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Standing Desk Prices, and Which Ones Rise High Enough</h2>
