              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">iMovR Lander, laminate</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,195 (47 in.) to $1,745 (77 in.) (iMovR)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not stated in store data</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not checked</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">iMovR sells height extenders, $75&ndash;$170</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            All prices 24 November 2026. The pattern is plain: the cheapest desks stop at about 46.5 inches, which by
            the formula suits users up to about 5 feet 5 inches on a slim pad. Spending $244 to $470 buys a three-stage
            desk reaching about 48.7 to 48.8 inches, enough for most users up to about 5 feet 9 inches. Getting to 50
            inches and beyond, which taller walkers need, costs about $580 and up. That is why our <a href="/best-treadmill-desks/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill desk roundup</a> only lists
            desks reaching about 50 inches or more.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Width between the legs matters as much as height</h3>
          <p>
            The pad has to fit between the desk&rsquo;s legs or feet with room to step on. The HOMELYM stand&rsquo;s
            listing gives 24.4 inches between its legs, which clears a 15-inch UREVO belt but is tight for a wide
            LifeSpan base at about 28 inches overall. iMovR says the Unsit needs at least 40 inches of free space between
            the lifting columns, and recommends desktops 53 inches wide or more. Four-leg desks are steadier, but the
            ones we priced stop low: FlexiSpot&rsquo;s 4-leg 71 x 32-inch desk ($295.99) reaches 47.2 inches and
            UPLIFT&rsquo;s V3 4-leg frame ($1,019) 47.7 inches, per their listings.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="integrated" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Integrated Treadmill Desk Prices</h2>
<p>
            An integrated treadmill desk is a walking base and desk designed and sold together. The usual extras are
            treadmill controls on or in the desk instead of a remote, a speed cap for safe working, and a single
            warranty. On 24 November 2026 these were the prices on the makers&rsquo; stores.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[680px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
